cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. A citation for the manuscript will be added when it is available."
type: software
title: "Evaluating Reproducibility in Retrieval-Augmented Scientific Question Answering for Bioinformatics"
abstract: >-
  Research software for a controlled study of how two representations of the same scientific
  publication (PubMed Central JATS XML and Docling-converted PDF) affect evidence preservation,
  retrieval, the context supplied to a generator, and scientific answer correctness in
  retrieval-augmented question answering for bioinformatics.
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Pudota
    given-names: Rama Krishna
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - scientific question answering
  - reproducibility
  - bioinformatics
  - document representation
